<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip Davis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1951">1951</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Brave Davis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip Davis, known as Brave Davis, is a Bahamian lawyer and politician who became prime minister of the Bahamas in September 2021. Leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/progressive-liberal-party">Progressive Liberal Party</a>, he had served as deputy prime minister under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthew-c-perry">Perry</a> Christie from 2012 to 2017 before leading the party to victory over Hubert Minnis's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-national-movement">Free National Movement</a> in the 2021 general election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-davis.jpg" alt="Philip Davis" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palácio do Planalto from Brasilia, Brasil · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Philip_%22Brave%22_Davis_(profile).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
